# command
netstat -at : The -a command retrieves active network connections and listening ports 
              while the -t command displays only TCP connections

# Observations
The command displayed current TCP, UDP connections,local,foreign addresses and their state, along
with offload data. In this way, active network connections can be monitored

For example; The state gives the status of a network connection such as ESTABLISHED OR LISTENING.
Thus, this information can be used to troubleshoot network issues


